        "keywords": "collgesuggest, top iit colleges in India, best iit colleges in India, top iit courses in India, list of top iit colleges in India, top colleges in India for iit, top 10 iit colleges in India, best 10 iit colleges in India, Top NITs , IIT, IIIT, GFTI, Government iit colleges, private iit colleges",
        "contents": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>So there will be 2 shifts for each session of the JEE main exam, the first shift exam time is from 9 am to 12 pm and the second shift is from 3 pm to 6pm, it is a good practice to reach the exam center at least one hour before the start time as it will give you enough time to settle down and get all the necessary documents to take into the center. Applicants will be allowed to enter the center at 8:30 am for the first shift and 2:30 pm for the second shift where the invigilator will give appropriate instructions and the candidates will start to read the instructions to login around 10 minutes prior to the starting of the exam time.</p>\n\n<table>\n\t<thead>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<th>Schedule of events</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Tentative JEE Main 2023 Session 1 dates</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Tentative JEE Main 2023 Session 2 dates</th>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</thead>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>1.Exam date</td>\n\t\t\t<td>24, 25, 27, 28, 29, 30 and 31 January 2023</td>\n\t\t\t<td>06, 08, 10, 11, 12 April 2023</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>2.JEE Main application window start date</td>\n\t\t\t<td>15 December 2022</td>\n\t\t\t<td>To be announced&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>3.JEE Main last date for filling application</td>\n\t\t\t<td>To be announced&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>To be announced&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>4.JEE Main exam admit card release</td>\n\t\t\t<td>Third week of the January 2023</td>\n\t\t\t<td>To be announced&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>5.Answer key for JEE Main exam release date&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>To be announced&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>To be announced&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>6.Results for JEE Main exam&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>To be announced&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>To be announced&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>JEE Main exam is conducted in 2 sessions and each session has 2 shifts each day- Shift 1from 9 am to 12 pm and Shift 2 is from 3pm to 6 pm.</li>\n\t<li>Some of the schedules that the candidates need to know about the JEE Main exam are</li>\n</ul>\n\n<table>\n\t<thead>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<th>Details</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Shift 1</th>\n\t\t\t<th>Shift 2&nbsp;</th>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</thead>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>1. Exam timing</td>\n\t\t\t<td>9 AM -12 PM&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>3 PM -6 PM</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>2. Candidate entry to the exam center</td>\n\t\t\t<td>08:30 AM&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>2:30 PM&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>3. Instructions given by the invigilator to candidates</td>\n\t\t\t<td>08:30 AM - 08:50 AM&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>2:30 AM- 2:50 PM</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>4. Login time</td>\n\t\t\t<td>08:50 AM&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>2:50 PM</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>5. JEE Main exam start time</td>\n\t\t\t<td>9 AM&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>3 PM</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>6. JEE Main exam end time</td>\n\t\t\t<td>12 PM&nbsp;</td>\n\t\t\t<td>6 PM</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>So there will be 2 shifts for each session of the JEE main exam, the first shift exam time is from 9 am to 12 pm and the second shift is from 3 pm to 6pm, it is a good practice to reach the exam center at least one hour before the start time as it will give you enough time to settle down and get all the necessary documents to take into the center. Applicants will be allowed to enter the center at 8:30 am for the first shift and 2:30 pm for the second shift where the invigilator will give appropriate instructions and the candidates will start to read the instructions to login around 10 minutes prior to the starting of the exam time.</p>\n",
